Theorem L-1: Per-dimension lattice algebra for the 7-dim product

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS product lattice has 7 dimensions per Annex E §AIMS + the canonical proof notation sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - Each dimension MUST be a finite lattice with explicit value set,
      partial-order axioms, join operation, and height
    - Per-dimension symbols are drawn from the canonical table in
      the canonical proof notation sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
      (parser rejects ad-hoc symbols per notation_unknown_symbol)
    - Product height SHALL equal sum of dimension heights per L-5

  Soundness property:
    The following 7 dimension structures define the AIMS product lattice:

      Access dimension:
        carrier = {B, O}
        ordering = B < O
        join = max
        height = 1
        canonical = totally ordered carrier

      Consumption dimension:
        carrier = {empty, L, A, U}
        ordering = empty < L < A < U
        join = max
        height = 3
        canonical = totally ordered carrier

      Cardinality dimension:
        carrier = {absent, 1, omega}
        ordering = absent < 1 < omega
        join = max (for alt_join at CFG merges per IA-3)
        seq_add = QTT semiring per Annex E §AIMS.3
                    (absent + x = x; 1 + 1 = omega; x + omega = omega)
        height = 2
        canonical = totally ordered carrier

      Uniqueness dimension:
        carrier = {u, ms, s}
        ordering = u < ms < s
        join = max
        height = 2
        canonical = totally ordered carrier

      Locality dimension:
        carrier = {bl, fl, ae, he, top}
        ordering = bl < fl < ae < he < top
        join = max (= seq_add = alt_join per Annex E §AIMS.5)
        height = 4
        canonical = totally ordered carrier

      Shape dimension:
        carrier = {Phi, R_S, R_V, C, H}
        ordering = flat lattice (no proper subordering)
        join = case_analysis: equal -> a; unequal -> Phi
        height = 1
        canonical = flat lattice with Phi as TOP

      Effect dimension:
        carrier = 3-bit flag product over {may_alloc, may_share, may_throw}
        ordering = componentwise Bool implication on each flag
        join = componentwise OR
        height = 3
        canonical = 3-flag product

    Product lattice total height:
      1 + 3 + 2 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 3 = 16 (matches Annex E §AIMS IA-7 CHAIN_HEIGHT)

    L-5 (finite height) holds: every dimension's carrier is finite + bounded.
    L-1, L-2, L-3 (commutativity, associativity, idempotence) discharged
    by sec-02 lattice algebra proofs against the per-dimension joins above.
    L-6 (monotonicity) holds for max-based dimensions trivially;
    Shape flat-lattice and Effect componentwise-OR are monotone.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-02 lattice algebra proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension algebraic-identity discharge)
      monotonicity (validates L-6 monotonicity preserved by per-dimension joins)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-02 discharges per-dimension lattice proofs
